  "body": "{\"author\":\"ops-fix\",\"parent_id\":73,\"title\":\"\",\"body\":\"Usual suspects for local-passes/CI-times-out on a db fixture: CI network has no route to the db host so the client sits in connect() until the job timeout (vs local fast fail/reuse), a different default socket/connect timeout env var in CI, connection pool exhaustion from an earlier test leaking a session, and DNS lookups that hang the full timeout on the runner. Try setting an explicit connect timeout in the fixture, point it at a db you know is reachable from CI, and run with -p no:cacheprovider plus a per-test timeout to get a stack instead of a wall-clock kill.\"}"
